<title>USA: Dialogic Q1 shr $0.20 vs $0.30 before gain.</title>
<headline>Dialogic Q1 shr $0.20 vs $0.30 before gain.</headline>
<dateline>PARSIPPANY, N.J. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>						  Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							March 31,</p>
<p>					     1997    %	1996     %</p>
<p> Revenues			     $57,089 100.0  $48,732  100.0</p>
<p> Operating income		     4,692   8.2    6,621   13.6</p>
<p> Interest income, Net		 (354)  (0.6)    (754)  (1.5)</p>
<p>Net realized losses (gains) on</p>
<p>  available for sale securities	4     --   (9,245) (19.0)</p>
<p>Income before provision for</p>
<p>  income taxes			  5,042   8.8   16,620   34.1</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	 1,815   3.1    6,008   12.3</p>
<p> Net income			    3,227   5.7    10,612(a)21.8</p>
<p> Income per share			 .20	     0.65(a)</p>
<p>Shares used in the calculation</p>
<p>  of income per share		16,511	   16,256</p>
<p>(a) Excluding gain of $0.35 per share on sale of Voice Control Systems stock, net income would have been $4.8 million and EPS would have been $0.30.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
